# D-Bus activation for the GNOME Shell search provider bus name. The app owns this
# name itself while running (DBusActivatable stays false in the .desktop - Tauri's
# GTK main is not a GApplication); this file only lets the bus LAUNCH the app when
# the shell queries while it is not running, after which the freshly started app
# claims the name. If activation races or fails, the shell simply skips the
# provider - it degrades, never blocks search.
# The internal flag keeps the configured main window hidden while GNOME/KRunner
# issue queries. Activating a result promotes that same process to the full app.
# Exec must be an absolute path for dbus-daemon; Flatpak rewrites it on export.
[D-BUS Service]
Name=tools.lolly.Desktop.SearchProvider
Exec=/usr/bin/lolly-desktop --search-provider
